# TUI UX & UI Design Rules

This document specifies the Terminal User Interface (TUI) architecture, keyboard navigation, and visual styling for `ytmusic-cli`.

---

## 1. Information Architecture & Layout Structure

The TUI maintains a consistent, three-zone visual layout across all screens:

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| Header: [App Title]                 [Active User / Network] |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                             |
| Screen Content Area:                                        |
|   - MainMenu / SearchScreen / PlaylistScreen / Settings     |
|   - Dynamic views mounted into main container               |
|                                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| Mini Player / Player Bar:                                   |
|   ▶ Track Title - Artist [01:45/03:30] [Vol: 80%] [==----]  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
| Footer: [q] Quit  [Space] Play/Pause  [/] Search  [?] Help  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
```

---

## 2. Keyboard-First Navigation Standards

1. **Global Keybindings**:
   - `q`: Quit the application (or exit current modal/subscreen).
   - `Space`: Toggle playback (Play / Pause).
   - `+` / `-`: Volume up / Volume down (in 5% increments).
   - `/`: Focus search input / open quick search.
   - `h` or `?`: Open Help modal overlay.
   - `Esc`: Cancel input, close modal, or navigate to previous screen.

2. **List & Selection Controls**:
   - `j` or `Down`: Move selection down.
   - `k` or `Up`: Move selection up.
   - `Enter`: Activate selected item (play track, open playlist, select menu).
   - `Tab` / `Shift+Tab`: Cycle through interactive widgets.

---

## 3. Visual Styling & TCSS Standards

1. **Color Palette & Semantic Tokens**:
   - Background Base: `#0F0F0F` (Dark terminal background).
   - Surface / Panels: `#1A1A1A` or `#222222`.
   - Brand / Primary Accent: `#FF0000` (YouTube Red).
   - Secondary Accent / Focus: `#3EA6FF` (YouTube Blue / Link color).
   - Text Primary: `#FFFFFF`.
   - Text Muted / Metadata: `#888888`.
   - Status Success: `#2BA640`.
   - Status Warning / Error: `#FF8800` / `#E53935`.

2. **Affordances & Focus States**:
   - Every interactive widget must have a distinct `:focus` state in `app.tcss`.
   - Focused list items must display visual highlight (background accent or `>` indicator).
   - Playing tracks must display an active badge or animated glyph (`▶` or `♫`).

3. **Terminal Size Adaptation**:
   - Minimum supported terminal dimension: 80 columns x 24 rows.
   - Graceful degradation: Collapsible ASCII banners on small screens (`height < 30`).
   - Use Textual's `LoadingIndicator` during async operations.

4. **Notifications & Feedback**:
   - For user feedback, use `self.notify(message, severity="info"|"warning"|"error")`.
   - Avoid silent failures; provide instant visual confirmation when an action starts and completes.
